<p>I was playing around with visualising the S&P 500 by market cap and decided to add employees to each company's bubble.<p>What surprised me was how empty some of the biggest companies looked.<p>Nvidia is worth $5.2 trillion but employs only 42,000 people. That's around $124 million in market cap per employee. Meanwhile, Accenture employs 814,000 people and is worth $146 billion.<p>Each stick figure represents 10,000 employees. You can zoom in and explore individual companies.<p>I wrote a bit more about what I found here: <a href="https://bigwhalehunting.com/blog/workforce/" rel="nofollow">https://bigwhalehunting.com/blog/workforce/</a><p>Would be interested to hear what you think.</p>
